const title = "Blaze Outdoor Grill Repair Los Angeles — Same Day";
const description = `Blaze grill and outdoor refrigerator repair across SoCal. Prelude LBM, Premium LTE, LUX, BLZ-SSRF fridge. Lifetime-warranty parts, you pay labor. ${phone}.`;

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Blaze has a lifetime warranty. Does that make repairs cheaper?",
    a: "Often yes, and this is the single most useful thing to know about owning a Blaze. Blaze covers the burners, cooking grates, grill body, flame tamers, heat zone separators, warming rack, and control valves for the lifetime of the original owner. The part is free. What that means in practice: when your Blaze burner or control valve fails, our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair help you claim the free warranty part, and you pay only our labor plus the $89 outdoor diagnostic. Ignition and lighting components carry a shorter one-year warranty, so those become standard paid parts after year one."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you fix Blaze outdoor refrigerators too?",
    a: "Yes. Blaze outdoor refrigerator repair is one of our common Blaze calls. We service the BLZ-SSRF line, from the 20-inch 4.3 and 4.5 cubic foot units to the 24-inch 5.5 cubic foot fridge and the 5.2 cubic foot double-drawer (BLZ-SSRF-50DH), all 304 stainless. The most common Blaze fridge jobs are door hinge alignment and gasket replacement (a warm-running fridge is very often a failed door seal, not a dead compressor), condenser coil cleaning, and thermostat faults. The refrigerator carries a one-year sealed-system warranty. EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410)."
  },
  {
    q: "My Blaze won't light with the push-and-turn ignition. What's wrong?",
    a: "Blaze uses a Push and Turn flame-thrower ignition with crossover channels between the burners, so the whole grill lights from one burner's flame. When it stops working, the failure is usually the ignition electrode or the battery on that lead burner, or a clogged crossover channel that stops the flame from carrying to the next burner. Our techs test the electrode, the crossover, and the gas flow in sequence. Ignition parts are covered one year, then paid, and they are inexpensive."
  },
  {
    q: "What Blaze grill models do you service?",
    a: "The full lineup. Prelude LBM (the value built-in, BLZ-3LBM and BLZ-4LBM in 25 and 32 inch), Premium LTE and LTE+ (the lit-knob mid line), the LTE Pro, the Professional LUX (the flagship), and the Marine grade. All of them use the 14,000 BTU commercial-style cast burners and the same crossover ignition, so the repair patterns carry across the line."
  },
  {
    q: "How long do Blaze grills last in Los Angeles?",
    a: "The lifetime warranty on the major components tilts the math heavily toward keeping and repairing a Blaze rather than replacing it, often 15 years and well beyond on the cast burners and body. Salt air is still the limiter here. On coastal installs in Malibu, Newport Beach, and Pacific Palisades, ignition electrodes and hardware corrode faster, but since the burners and valves are warranty-covered for life, the ongoing cost of a coastal Blaze is mostly our labor, not parts."
  },
  {
    q: "My Blaze is built into an island. Does that change the repair?",
    a: "Access changes, the diagnosis does not. Our techs service the built-in Prelude LBM, Premium LTE, and Professional LUX from the front of a Beverly Hills or Bel Air BBQ island, swapping burners, flame tamers, and control valves without pulling the grill out of the surround. On LP setups we confirm the regulator and gas line before re-firing. $89 outdoor diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "Can you get the free warranty part for me, or do I have to?",
    a: "We help. On a lifetime-covered Blaze component, we identify the exact part, document the failure, and coordinate the warranty replacement so you are not chasing it yourself. Blaze provides the part at no cost to the original owner; you cover shipping and our labor. It is a genuinely owner-friendly warranty, and knowing how to work it is part of what we bring to a Blaze repair."
  },
  {
    q: "What's your warranty on Blaze repairs?",
    a: "Ninety days SDAR parts-and-labor warranty on the work we perform, on top of whatever Blaze factory warranty covers the component itself. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified, and BBB Accredited Business."
  }
];

