<!-- 01 INTRO -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Blaze service</p>
    <h2>The Blaze warranty changes the repair math, and we know how to work it.</h2>

    <p><strong>When a Blaze grill fails at an LA home, the first thing our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair check is whether the failed part is lifetime-covered. Blaze warranties the burners, cooking grates, body, flame tamers, heat zone separators, warming rack, and control valves for the life of the original owner. On those failures the part is free, and you pay only our labor plus the $89 outdoor diagnostic. Ignition and lighting are covered one year, then standard paid parts. Grill or BLZ-SSRF outdoor fridge, we service both. $89 outdoor diagnostic, waived with repair. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), BBB Accredited.</strong></p>

    <p class="intro-speakable">Blaze Outdoor Products built its reputation on giving near-premium hardware, commercial-style 14,000 BTU cast burners and heavy 304 stainless, at a price well under Lynx or Twin Eagles, and then backing the major components with a lifetime warranty. For an owner, that warranty is the whole story: a Blaze is one of the cheapest premium-grade grills to keep running for the long haul, because the expensive parts are covered and the recurring cost is mostly labor.</p>

    <p>Our techs service the full Blaze grill lineup: the value-built Prelude LBM (BLZ-3LBM and BLZ-4LBM), the Premium LTE and LTE+ with lit control knobs, the LTE Pro, the flagship Professional LUX, and the Marine grade. On the cold side we handle the BLZ-SSRF outdoor refrigeration line, from the 20-inch 4.3 and 4.5 cubic foot units to the 24-inch 5.5 cubic foot fridge and the SSRF-50DH drawer. One brand, one visit, grill and cold storage both.</p>

    <p>BHGS #A49573. Same-day across LA, Orange County, Ventura. We handle the Blaze warranty claim so you do not have to.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 BLAZE LINEUP -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">Lineup and architecture</p>
    <h2>The Blaze lineup and what fails on each.</h2>

    <p class="lead">Blaze grills share one engineering platform across price points: commercial-style 14,000 BTU cast burners, a Push-and-Turn flame-thrower ignition, and crossover channels that let the whole grill light from a single burner. That shared design means the repair patterns carry from the Prelude up to the LUX.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Prelude LBM (value built-in, BLZ-3LBM / BLZ-4LBM)</h3>
    <p>The entry built-in, 25-inch 3-burner and 32-inch 4-burner. Same 14,000 BTU cast burners as the pricier lines, simpler trim. Most common Prelude work is ignition (electrode or battery on the lead burner) and crossover-channel cleaning. Because the burners and valves are lifetime-covered, most Prelude repairs after year one are labor-only.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Premium LTE and LTE+ (mid line, lit knobs)</h3>
    <p>The Premium LTE adds illuminated control knobs and heavier build. The lit-knob LEDs are a common minor complaint (they are on the ignition-and-lighting side, one-year warranty), while the burners, grates, and valves underneath carry the lifetime coverage. We diagnose the LED and control circuit separately from the gas system.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">LTE Pro and Professional LUX (flagship)</h3>
    <p>The Professional LUX is the top of the Blaze line, thicker stainless, higher-output burners, and the same crossover ignition. The LUX runs hard at estate installs and shows more flame-tamer and heat-zone-separator wear from heavy use, both lifetime-covered parts. We replace them under warranty and bill only labor.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Ignition system (Push-and-Turn flame-thrower, crossover channels)</h3>
    <p>Blaze lights with a push-and-turn flame-thrower on the lead burner, and crossover channels carry the flame to the rest. A grill that will not light is usually the lead-burner electrode, its battery, or a crossover channel clogged with grease or corrosion that stops the flame from carrying. These are inexpensive, one-year-warranty parts. We test electrode, crossover, and gas flow in order rather than guessing.</p>

    <h3 class="series-h3">Blaze outdoor refrigeration (BLZ-SSRF line)</h3>
    <p>Blaze outdoor refrigerator repair is a steady part of our Blaze work. The BLZ-SSRF line runs from the 20-inch 4.3 and 4.5 cubic foot units to the 24-inch 5.5 cubic foot fridge and the SSRF-50DH drawer, all 304 stainless with a one-year sealed-system warranty. The single most common Blaze fridge symptom, a warm-running box, is usually a door out of alignment or a failed gasket, not a dead compressor. We check the door, hinge, and seal first, then the condenser coil, then the sealed system. Honest diagnosis before any expensive assumption.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 TYPICAL SCENARIOS -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Common scenarios</p>
    <h2>Top Blaze repairs in our 5-county territory.</h2>

    <p>Ranked by how often our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair see them across LA homes and the coast, most common first.</p>

    <ol class="num-list">
      <li><strong>Won't light (flame-thrower ignition).</strong> Lead-burner electrode or battery, or a clogged crossover channel. Test in sequence, replace the electrode or clean the crossover. One-year part, inexpensive.</li>
      <li><strong>Blaze fridge running warm.</strong> Door alignment and gasket first on the BLZ-SSRF, then condenser coil, then sealed system. Most are a door fix, not a compressor.</li>
      <li><strong>Control valve failure (lifetime-covered).</strong> Knob won't hold flame or won't turn. We claim the free warranty valve and bill only labor.</li>
      <li><strong>Flame tamer / heat zone separator wear (lifetime-covered).</strong> Burned-through tamers on high-use LUX and LTE grills. Warranty part, labor-only.</li>
      <li><strong>Burner replacement (lifetime-covered).</strong> Coastal corrosion or a cracked cast burner. Free warranty burner, our labor to install.</li>
      <li><strong>Lit-knob LED failure (Premium LTE).</strong> Illuminated control knob out. Diagnose the LED and control circuit separately from the gas side.</li>
      <li><strong>Crossover channel corrosion.</strong> Flame won't carry between burners on coastal installs. Clean or replace the crossover.</li>
      <li><strong>Fridge door gasket and hinge.</strong> Warm BLZ-SSRF from a failed seal. Gasket and hinge alignment.</li>
      <li><strong>Cook grate service.</strong> Cast grates on coastal grills. Lifetime-covered, labor to swap.</li>
      <li><strong>Fridge thermostat / fan.</strong> Temperature drift on the SSRF line after the condenser is ruled out.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 REAL REPAIR STORIES -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-number">Real repairs</p>
    <h2>Composite stories from the route.</h2>

    <p class="lead">Five Blaze jobs typical of the past 90 days. Models, symptoms, diagnosis, time, total. Names omitted; the scenarios are what we see weekly.</p>

    <div class="story-grid">
      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Irvine, Blaze Professional LUX (2019 install)</h3>
        <p>Two control knobs would not hold a flame. Diagnosis: two failed control valves, both lifetime-covered. We documented the failure, claimed the free warranty valves, and installed them. Owner paid only labor plus diagnostic. Total: $89 plus 1.25 hours labor, parts $0 under warranty.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Malibu, Blaze Prelude LBM BLZ-4LBM (2021 install)</h3>
        <p>Grill would not light at all. Coastal install, 4 years of salt air. Diagnosis: corroded lead-burner electrode plus a crossover channel clogged with grease so the flame never carried. Replaced the electrode, cleaned the crossovers, tested full light-off. Total: $89 plus $60 part plus 45 minutes = $224.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Newport Beach, Blaze BLZ-SSRF 5.5 fridge (2020 install)</h3>
        <p>"Fridge is warm, compressor sounds fine." Diagnosis: door sagging on a worn hinge, gasket no longer sealing, cold air spilling out. Realigned the door, replaced the gasket, verified pull-down to temperature. No sealed-system work needed. Total: $89 plus $95 part plus 1 hour = $274.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Beverly Hills, Blaze Premium LTE (2018 install)</h3>
        <p>Burned-through flame tamers and one cracked cast burner at heavy use. Both lifetime-covered. Claimed the warranty tamers and burner, installed them, and re-seasoned the grill. Owner paid labor only. Total: $89 plus 1.5 hours labor, parts $0 under warranty.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="story-card">
        <h3>Pacific Palisades, Blaze Prelude LBM (2017 install)</h3>
        <p>Multiple coastal issues at 8 years: two corroded burners, worn cook grates, dead ignition on one zone. Burners and grates were warranty parts; only the ignition electrode was a paid part. Did all of it in one visit. Total: $89 plus $55 electrode plus 2 hours labor, the rest $0 under warranty.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 HONEST SCOPE -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">Scope</p>
    <h2>What we do for Blaze, and what we don't.</h2>

    <p><strong>We service:</strong></p>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>All Blaze built-in gas grills (Prelude LBM, Premium LTE and LTE+, LTE Pro, Professional LUX, Marine)</li>
      <li>Push-and-Turn flame-thrower ignition and crossover-channel systems</li>
      <li>Lifetime-covered components: burners, cooking grates, body, flame tamers, heat zone separators, warming rack, control valves (warranty claim handled by us)</li>
      <li>Blaze outdoor refrigeration (BLZ-SSRF 4.3, 4.5, 5.5 cubic foot, and SSRF-50DH drawer)</li>
      <li>Fridge door gasket, hinge alignment, condenser, and thermostat service</li>
      <li>Cook grates, flame tamers, and burner replacement under warranty</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>We don't do:</strong> new Blaze grill or refrigerator installation (fabrication and gas-line trade, not appliance repair); custom island or cabinetry modification; sealed-system refrigerant recharge on outdoor fridges that ship without a service port (against replacement cost it rarely makes sense, and we will tell you so).</p>

    <p>Because so many Blaze components are lifetime-covered, our first step on most Blaze repairs is confirming whether the part is a free warranty claim. If it is, you pay only our labor and the diagnostic. That is the honest advantage of owning a Blaze, and working it correctly is part of our service.</p>
  </div>
</section>

